job.description:
Position: Data Engineer (m/f/d)
Location: Remote
Contract: Long-term with a 3-month trial period
Format: Freelance; full time

Our customers, large German corporations, DAX companies, and medium-sized businesses, need highly skilled and ambitious data engineers who are enthusiastic about using data throughout their entire value chain.

What tasks do you expect?

● Setting up the cloud infrastructure for data science applications;
● Conception and development of data models, data pipelines and meaningful visualizations / dashboards;
● Development and optimization of data management strategies, workflows and infrastructure for data collection and use in close cooperation with the team;
● Support for error tracking and data quality reporting

That's what makes you stand out:

● 2+ years of experience as a data engineer;
● Sound knowledge and practical experience with Azure and/or AWS;
● Expertise in data warehousing;
● Very good knowledge of SQL, Python;
● Extensive experience with databases, ETL/ data pipelines, data modeling, APIs
● Business fluent German and English language skills (at least B2 language level)

Not mandatory, but definitely desirable:

● Experience with DevOps, Apache Spark, Apache Airflows, Agile;
● Expertise in API Gateways, Oracle, Microservices, Power BI / Tableau, Celonis, AWS
Sagemaker, ML/ AI Algorithms, Kafka, On Premise ETL Pipelines, Business Tools

We offer you these benefits:

● Rewarding work experience, industry diversity;
● Competitive and attractive salary;
● Opportunity to work from home;
● Project duration: 9+ months on average
